      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Carleton College, originally Northfield College, opened in 1866 under the Minnesota Conference of Congregational churches, a legacy of the town’s Yankee founders.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northfield%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Olaf College began in 1874 on Northfield’s western edge, founded by Norwegian Lutheran pastors and farmers dedicated to preserving their faith and culture.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northfield%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "On September 7, 1876, the James-Younger Gang attempted to rob Northfield’s First National Bank, a dramatic moment in the town’s history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northfield%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Peter Agre, a Nobel Prize–winning chemist, was born in Northfield, making the town the hometown of a world‑renowned scientist.",
